  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A group organizer can share interests, and the museum can describe available rooms and volunteer times.\", \"decision\": \"How should the museum prepare for a visiting group?\", \"goal\": \"Help visitors find a satisfying route through the museum while keeping reception and volunteers manageable.\", \"problem\": \"A volunteer-run local museum wants to make a weekend visit easier to navigate. It has a modest collection, printed guides, a reception table, flexible volunteer positions, and several rooms that can remain open independently. The decisions concern interpretation and visitor organization, not conservation rules or safety policy.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe organizer shares interests before the museum proposes rooms and volunteer times. The proposed visit begins with the group’s purposes.\nThe museum describes rooms and volunteer times before the organizer chooses a focus. The organizer plans within visible opportunities.\nThe organizer and museum compare interests, rooms, and volunteer times in one planning call. The visit is assembled through simultaneous negotiation."
    }
